{{Quote|There's something here, inside that mountain.|[[Hunter]]|<ref name="War-Mantle" />}}
The '''Imperial Base on Daro'''<ref name="Base DB">{{Databank|imperial-base-on-daro|Imperial Base on Daro}}</ref> was a secret [[Galactic Empire]] training facility located on the otherwise-uninhabited [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Daro]] shortly after the Empire's [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]]. Hidden inside of a [[mountain]], the base was situated around a large central ring, with [[turbolift]]s that connected to each level. It had several [[hangar]]s, and its muster report included fifty [[Cloning|clone]] Imperial [[commando]]s and 1,000 [[TK stormtrooper|TK troopers]]. Shortly after the Empire's formation, the rogue [[clone commando]]s known as the [[Clone Force 99|Bad Batch]] entered the base to [[Extraction on Daro|rescue]] [[Gregor]], a commando who had attempted to [[Desertion|desert]] from the facility.<ref name="War-Mantle" />

==History==
In [[19 BBY]], the newly-fledged Galactic Empire had begun looking for a more cost-effective alternative to the [[clone trooper]]s, who at the time formed the backbone of the [[Imperial Army]]. With the initiation of [[Project War-Mantle]], 1,000 "[[TK stormtrooper|TK troopers]]" were enlisted and sent to be trained at the Imperial Base on Daro. There, the recruits were instructed and trained by a contingent of 50 Imperial clone commandos, while also providing security for the base.<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref>

[[Clone Force 99]], having been tasked by their contact, [[Rex|Captain Rex]], to save a rogue commando named [[Gregor]] from the base, landed on the planet and infiltrated the facility. Not long after breaking Gregor out of captivity, the team was compromised by a clone commando and his squad of TK troopers, though they were swiftly dispatched. The extraction team ran through the facility, and engaged numerous TK troopers and their clone instructors in intense firefights. Eventually, the team managed to extract through the base's reactor port, but the squad's leader, [[Hunter]], slipped and plummeted off the mountainside of the base. Though he survived, he was surrounded by Imperial troops and captured.<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref>

